<% page_title "Privacy" %>

<article class="prose-market max-w-2xl">
  <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-paper">Privacy</h1>
  <p>This site is a public list of hardware that runs Omarchy. Anyone running Omarchy can send a report of their machine, and reports are public once they arrive. No account is needed.</p>
  <p>A report holds the vendor and model, CPU, memory size, GPU names, UEFI, TPM and Secure Boot state, and the Omarchy version. It does not hold serial numbers, board serials, MAC addresses, hostnames, usernames, or product UUIDs. The collector and the server both refuse those fields.</p>
  <p>The script hashes machine-id and DMI serials in memory and sends only that digest, so the same machine updates one row instead of creating many. The digest cannot be turned back into the machine-id. Submitter IP addresses are stored only as a salted hash, for abuse control, and are never shown.</p>
  <p>If you run the script on a machine that is not running Omarchy, it checks that machine on your computer and sends nothing unless you answer yes. A yes sends the same hardware facts, the verdict, and the name of your distro, as a candidate report. Candidates are never shown or counted on public pages. You are only told how many machines of that model have reported running Omarchy.</p>
  <p>Only people who run the collector on Omarchy create public reports. Admins can see every report and the challenge records that guard submissions. Admin accounts store an email address; nobody else has an account.</p>
</article>
